  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moving On Through Enterprise/Ukuqubekeka Phambili Ngeshishini</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The levels of poverty in South Africa are particularly high for the homeless and long term unemployed. A lack of basic skills makes it even more difficult for people to move from long term unemployment to employment. A solution to this problem has been developed by the applicant in partnership with its sister organisation in South Africa and the Big Issue South Africa. The proposal focuses on a programme which provides skills and sales training to Big Issue sellers. This has already resulted in increased sales for participating sellers and an increase to 50% of those moving onto other forms of permanent employment or self-run enterprises. This project seeks to build on a successful pilot in Cape Town and extend the training programmes to support more individuals into employment or self employment. One key area of growth will be the establishment of a Big Issue Cafe to promote and provide nutritious food, provide work experience for Big Issue vendors, small business development and a sustainable income for the project. Two similar Cafes have already been started by the applicant in South Africa to provide sustainability for core staff and programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
